1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,768
What if Pluto replaced our Moon?

2
00:00:02,283 --> 00:00:06,199
Pluto is about 2003 hundred and seventy-seven kilometers wide.

3
00:00:06,199 --> 00:00:10,999
About two-thirds the width of our Moon, so it would look smaller in the sky.

4
00:00:11,483 --> 00:00:15,907
But it's coated in bright ices, and reflects roughly six times more light.

5
00:00:15,907 --> 00:00:19,553
By our rough math, a full Pluto could outshine the full Moon.

6
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:22,676
Pluto has only about a sixth of the Moon's mass.

7
00:00:22,676 --> 00:00:25,083
So its tides would be weaker than the Sun's.

8
00:00:25,583 --> 00:00:27,533
Like and subscribe for more what-ifs.

9
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:32,370
And sunlight here is about fifteen hundred times stronger than out at Pluto.

10
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:34,996
Its nitrogen ice would start turning to gas.

11
00:00:35,483 --> 00:00:40,842
Its big moon Charon is half Pluto's size, and they circle each other every 6.4 days.

12
00:00:40,842 --> 00:00:44,287
This close to Earth, the pair might not stay together.

13
00:00:44,783 --> 00:00:46,578
So what if we had no Moon at all?

14
00:00:46,578 --> 00:00:47,992
Full story on the channel.
